== Z1. zdb_rig_code, and what each rig makes of zdb's exit code (old = 09860a0, new = 9710a24)
  At the end (zdb -bcc): the reference judge's exit with a pool left and nothing else / with no pool left;
  the daemon judge's exit with nothing else. In the main pass (zdb -bbbbb): the failure every_copy_verdict
  writes, the reference exit with a pool left, and the daemon's classify.
     rc rig code | end: ref, left ref, no left    daemon | main pass failure                ref, left   daemon
      0    False |              2            0         0 | None                                  None     None
      1    False |              1            1         1 | copies: zdb                              1  failure
      2    False |              1            1         1 | copies: zdb                              1  failure
    124     True |              2            1         2 | rig: zdb timed out                       2      rig
    127     True |              2            1         2 | rig: zdb could not start                 2      rig
    134    False |              1            1         1 | copies: zdb                              1  failure
    135    False |              1            1         1 | copies: zdb                              1  failure
    137    False |              1            1         1 | copies: zdb                              1  failure
    139    False |              1            1         1 | copies: zdb                              1  failure
     -6    False |              1            1         1 | rig: zdb died with signal 6              1  failure
     -7     True |           1->2            1      1->2 | rig: zdb died with signal 7              2      rig
     -9     True |           1->2            1      1->2 | rig: zdb died with signal 9              2      rig
    -11     True |           1->2            1      1->2 | rig: zdb died with signal 11             2      rig
    -15     True |           1->2            1      1->2 | rig: zdb died with signal 15             2      rig
  None: zdb_rig_code False; the daemon judge: (2, ['zdb -bcc did not run on the final image'])

== Z2. What run() gives for a signal, directly and through a shell
  SIGABRT: the command itself -6 (rig code False); a wrapper's exit 134 (rig code False)
  SIGKILL: the command itself -9 (rig code True); a wrapper's exit 137 (rig code False)
  SIGSEGV: the command itself -11 (rig code True); a wrapper's exit 139 (rig code False)
  SIGBUS: the command itself -7 (rig code True); a wrapper's exit 135 (rig code False)
  Both rigs run zdb as run(['zdb', ...]), never through a shell.

== Z3. The daemon judge stopped by the rig's own error after zdb -bcc ran (check(), its except path)
  zdb -bcc rc   -9: stopped path exit 1, says "a verdict against the daemon"; the same rc where the run ends normally: 2
  zdb -bcc rc  -11: stopped path exit 1, says "a verdict against the daemon"; the same rc where the run ends normally: 2
  zdb -bcc rc   -6: stopped path exit 1, says "a verdict against the daemon"; the same rc where the run ends normally: 1
  zdb -bcc rc  124: stopped path exit 2, says the rig's error; the same rc where the run ends normally: 2
  zdb -bcc rc    0: stopped path exit 2, says the rig's error; the same rc where the run ends normally: 2

